* CHARMM 32 testcase sccgsbp6_2cba.inp
* .Test that GSBP refuses to evaluate SCC-DFTB against a static external
* .field that does not exist, instead of reading it anyway.  This is what
* .bucknerj/dev#60 died of.  Same carbonic anhydrase system as
* .sccgsbp4_2cba.inp, no dynamics.
* .Author: Josh Buckner, 2026
*

IF ?SCCDFTB .NE. 1 THEN
 echo "c32test/sccgsbp6_2cba> SCCDFTB Test NOT performed."
 STOP
endif

IF ?QGSBP .NE. 1 THEN
 echo "c32test/sccgsbp6_2cba> GSBP Test NOT performed."
 STOP
endif

bomb -5

! variables
stream datadir.def

! SCC-DFTB needs SCCDFTB_DATA pointing at a directory holding this test's
! parameter file.  `genv' on an unset variable is a level-0 warning, which is
! fatal at the default BOMLEV, so lower BOMLEV across the call and self-skip
! when the data has not been provisioned here.  The file check matters as
! well: SCCDFTB_DATA can be set while this particular file is absent, and
! CHARMM then dies part way through reading parameters with no termination
! line at all.
set sccdftbdir UNSET_SCCDFTB_DATA
set oldbomlev ?bomlev
bomlev -5
genv sccdftbdir SCCDFTB_DATA
bomlev @oldbomlev
if @sccdftbdir eq UNSET_SCCDFTB_DATA then
   echo SCCGSBP6_2CBA TESTCASE RESULT: SKIP
   stop
endif
strc sccdat @sccdftbdir "/sccdftb_ONCHZN.dat"
bomlev -5
open unit 98 read form name @sccdat
if ?iostat .ne. 1 then
   echo SCCGSBP6_2CBA TESTCASE RESULT: SKIP
   stop
endif
close unit 98
bomlev @oldbomlev

set j    2cba
set k    2cba_gsbp
! Build what this testcase reads.  The scratch directory is cleared before
! every testcase, so nothing another testcase wrote is here.  This writes a
! PHIX file as well, which this testcase then deliberately does not read --
! it is the shared setup, and generating MIJ on its own would not be
! cheaper.
stream @0sccgsbp_matrices.str
stream @0sccgsbp_system.str
stream @0sccgsbp_cons.str

OPEN UNIT 21 NAME @0top_ca.inp READ FORM
READ RTF card UNIT 21
CLOSE UNIT 21

OPEN UNIT 22 NAME @0par_ca.inp READ FORM
READ PARA card UNIT 22
CLOSE UNIT 22

OPEN UNIT 3 NAME @9@k_sb.psf READ  FORM
READ  PSF CARD UNIT 3
CLOSE UNIT 3

OPEN UNIT 3 NAME @9@k_sb.crd READ FORM
READ  COOR CARD UNIT 3
CLOSE UNIT 3

NBONDS  GROUP  SWITCH CDIE  VDW VSWI  EXTEND GRAD QUAD -
        CUTNB 13.0  CTOFNB 12.0 CTONNB 8.0  WMIN 1.5  EPS 1.0 -
        inbfrq -1

set rsphere 20.0              ! radius of the spherical region of interest

! center of active site (at zinc atom)
set xcen   0.0
set ycen   0.0
set zcen   0.0

define INNER   sele POINT @xcen @ycen @zcen CUT @rsphere end

! We don't need to consider the bare Coulombic interactions between IR and OR
! because it is already incorporated into PHIX.
SCALAR CHARGE SET 0.0 sele .not. INNER end

! -------------- SCC section ----------------
define qm sele (segid 2CBA .and. -
! imidazole groups from nearby histidine residues
       (resid 94 .or. resid 92 .or. resid 117) .and. .not. -
       (type CA .or. type C .or. type N .or. type O -
        .or. type HN .or. type HA)) -
! link atoms
       .or. (segid 2CBA .and. type QQ*) .or. -
! Zn and Zn-bound water
       (segid SOLV .and. resid 1) .or. (segid ZNAT .and. type ZN) SHOW end

scalar WMAIN set 1.0 sele (qm) .and. type O*  SHOW end
scalar WMAIN set 2.0 sele (qm) .and. type N*  SHOW end
scalar WMAIN set 3.0 sele (qm) .and. type C*  SHOW end
scalar WMAIN set 4.0 sele (qm) .and. type H*  SHOW end
scalar WMAIN set 4.0 sele (qm) .and. type QQ*  SHOW end
scalar WMAIN set 5.0 sele (qm) .and. type ZN*  SHOW end

SCCDFTB remove CHRG +2 SELE qm END TEMP 0.00 SCFT 0.00000001 mull DATF @sccdat

! Single point energy must be performed in order to use sorting with SCCGSBP.
energy

!Now set GSBP up with the reaction-field matrices and nothing else.
!
! Note what is deliberately absent: no READ PHIX.  GSBP is perfectly willing
! to be set up this way, and the MM side of it asks whether the static
! external field is there before reading it -- QGAB and QPHIX gate the call
! to RFORCE2.  The SCC-DFTB side asked nothing, and handed the array that was
! never allocated straight to the interpolation in SCCGSBP0, which reads the
! potential at the eight grid points around every QM atom.  It arrives there
! as an assumed-size dummy carrying no bounds, so there was nothing to catch
! it and the run ended in a segmentation fault with no message of any kind.
!
! The same state is reached the way the report reached it -- leaving a GSBP
! setup in place across a change of system, so that the allocation block in
! PREP2 is skipped -- but that route needs a second molecule and a stream
! file that forgets to reset.  Asking for the boundary potential without the
! field it is read from is the same question in one command.
PBEQ

OPEN READ FILE UNIT 50 NAME @9@k_MIJ2.dat
READ MIJ UNIT 50
CLOSE UNIT 50

PRNLEV 8
GSBP SPHERE -
     NMPOL  2        MAXNPOL 4     -
     SRDIST @rsphere RRXCEN  @xcen RRYCEN @ycen RRZCEN @zcen
PRNLEV 5
END

SKIP All Excl QMEL ELEC GSBP

! Demote the refusal so the run survives it and this testcase can say what it
! did.  This is also the case the refusal has to be written for: a guard that
! only called WRNDIE would be demoted here too and carry straight on into the
! read it exists to prevent.
bomlev -6
ENER
bomlev @oldbomlev

! No field to read, so no GSBP energy.  This zero is the refusal and nothing
! else: the atoms are at their own coordinates and inside the region of
! interest, so the reaction-field half would otherwise contribute.  Without
! the refusal the run does not reach the next line at all.
@testcheck ?gsbp 0.0 -0.000001 sccgsbp6_2cba_no_field

SKIP NONE

set cfinal = FAIL
if @testfail eq 0 then set cfinal = PASS
echo SCCGSBP6_2CBA TESTCASE RESULT: @cfinal

STOP
